# Experiment 3: NumPy Boolean masks, filtering, and broadcasting

## ex3.code

```python
"""Experiment 3: NumPy Boolean masks, filtering, and broadcasting."""
import numpy as np

marks = np.array(
    [
        [72, 81, 69],
        [91, 77, 88],
        [64, 70, 75],
        [85, 93, 90],
    ]
)
subject_bonus = np.array([5, 0, 3])

print("Original marks:\n", marks)
print("\nBoolean mask for marks >= 80:\n", marks >= 80)
print("\nFiltered marks >= 80:", marks[marks >= 80])
print("\nRows whose average is at least 80:\n", marks[marks.mean(axis=1) >= 80])
print("\nSubject bonus broadcast across every student:\n", marks + subject_bonus)
```

