# Experiment 10: Grouped data with multiple aggregations

## ex10.code

```python
"""Experiment 10: Perform several aggregations on grouped data."""
import pandas as pd

students = pd.DataFrame(
    {
        "department": ["CSE", "ECE", "CSE", "ME", "ECE", "CSE", "ME"],
        "student": ["Asha", "Ben", "Charu", "Dev", "Eva", "Farhan", "Gita"],
        "marks": [88, 76, 93, 69, 84, 81, 90],
        "attendance": [96, 88, 99, 81, 93, 90, 95],
    }
)

summary = students.groupby("department").agg(
    student_count=("student", "count"),
    marks_mean=("marks", "mean"),
    marks_min=("marks", "min"),
    marks_max=("marks", "max"),
    attendance_mean=("attendance", "mean"),
)
print("Student records:\n", students)
print("\nMultiple grouped aggregations:\n", summary.round(2))
```

